<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank breakdown of west, east German GDP.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank breakdown of west, east German GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Real West German GDP was unchanged in the fourth quarter of 1996 versus the third quarter at 697.5 billion marks, the Bundesbank said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Bundesbank breakdown of west, east German GDP</p>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the following details of Q4 1996 GDP data:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN GDP   Q4 96    Q3 96	  Q2 96</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    -0.0     +1.0	   -1.5</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	 1.6     +1.9	   +1.1</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)    770.4    772.0	  765.8</p>
<p> WEST-GERMAN GDP   Q4 96   Q3 96	  Q2 96</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    -0.0     +0.5	   +1.0</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+1.5     +1.7	   +0.9</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)    697.5    698.8	  686.4</p>
<p> EAST-GERMAN GDP   Q4 96   Q3 96	  Q2 96</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    -0.5     +1.5	   +5.5</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+3.6     +3.8	   +2.9</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)     72.9     73.1	   72.1</p>
<p>NOTE - The year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from the Bundesbank GDP data. The figures are seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
